---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { Header } from '../components/layout/Header';
import Footer from '../components/layout/Footer.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy — SecurePass"
  description="SecurePass privacy: passwords are generated locally and never stored, synced, or transmitted."
  canonicalPath="/privacy"
>
  <Header client:load />
  <main class="mx-auto w-full max-w-3xl px-4 py-10 sm:px-6">
    <h1 class="text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-zinc-900 sm:text-3xl dark:text-zinc-50">Privacy</h1>
    <div class="mt-6 space-y-6 text-sm leading-relaxed text-zinc-600 sm:text-base dark:text-zinc-400">
      <p class="rounded-xl border border-emerald-200 bg-emerald-50 px-4 py-3 font-medium text-emerald-900 dark:border-emerald-900 dark:bg-emerald-950/40 dark:text-emerald-200">
        Your passwords are generated locally in your browser. They are not sent to our servers.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-zinc-900 dark:text-zinc-50">What we collect</h2>
      <p>
        Nothing. SecurePass has no accounts, no analytics, no tracking pixels, and no
        third-party scripts that can observe generated passwords. There is no server
        component that could receive your data in the first place.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-zinc-900 dark:text-zinc-50">What is stored on your device</h2>
      <ul class="list-disc space-y-2 pl-5">
        <li>
          <strong>Theme preference only.</strong> If you pick light, dark, or system theme,
          that single preference is saved in your browser’s local storage so the choice
          persists. Nothing else is written there.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Generated passwords are never stored.</strong> Not in local storage, session
          storage, cookies, the page URL, or browser history. The optional history feature
          keeps entries in the page’s memory only and wipes them when you reload or close
          the tab.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-zinc-900 dark:text-zinc-50">Network activity</h2>
      <p>
        After the page loads, SecurePass makes no network requests of its own. Copying a
        password uses your operating system’s clipboard; nothing about the password is
        transmitted.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-zinc-900 dark:text-zinc-50">Hosting</h2>
      <p>
        This is a static site — plain HTML, CSS, and JavaScript files. The hosting provider
        necessarily sees standard web-server logs (like any website), but the application
        itself sends it nothing about your passwords.
      </p>
    </div>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</BaseLayout>
